## 3. ROS2 Communication

a. Which ROS2 node should act as a publisher and which should act as a subscriber when sending the LED command?
- The user interface (ROS2 Node 2) node should be the publisher, it takes the user input and publishes the command to the topic LED control.
And the Serial bridge node (ROS2 Node 1) should be the subscriber, which will receive command from the tpic and then command the Arduino.

b. Which ROS2 node should publish the sensor values?
- The serial bridge node (ROS2 Node 1) should publish the sensor values as /sensor_data/value_a, /sensor_data/value_b, /sensor_data/value_c, /sensor_data/value_d.

c. Explain the difference between a ROS2 topic, publisher, and subscriber.
- Topic- A communication channel, through which Nodes exchange messages in specific format (ex: std_msgs/msg/Int64). Which also have specific name.
- publisher- A feature of Node, which produces and sends data to specific topic.
- Subscriber- A feature of Node, which listens to publisher and receives data when the publisher sends data.

